From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: roberth <roberth@arista.com>
Date: Mon, 18 Mar 2024 12:32:50 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Inject Aboot initrd and kernel

This patch adds the Aboot initrd and kernel to the BIOS. A new package
(AbootBinPkg) is created to manage the build of the binary image. This image is
built into the DXE firmware volume on SPI flash. The DXE firmware volume has a
hash included in the FDM and is authenticated by FdmVerify; therefore the chain
of trust is maintained. The Aboot image is identified in the DXE FV by a fixed
GUID (gAbootFileGuid) that I've generated.

In the past (Aboot11), this has been done by replacing the UEFI shell binary
with the Aboot image. Creating a separate package has the advantage that it
avoids the CRC calculation that is performed over the UEFI shell binary. This
check is not necessary for the Aboot image. The method also gives us slightly
more control over the locations that the BIOS searches for the image.

Code is added to enumerate the Aboot boot option in the boot option list.

Normally, in the BDS phase, H2O  will loop over the list of boot options,
trying each one until a boot option is launched successfully. In our case, for
security reasons, we want to *always* boot the Aboot image and *only* that
image. Therefore this patch replaces the normal boot option loop with code that
locates the Aboot boot option in the list and only tries that option. If boot
fails, the system will enter a CpuDeadLoop.
